rsistence afterward. This matches the fixed after-prepare/after-executor boot-identity cross-check (node1 ebd78841->428d4ad0, node2 a8b262d7->cbcb28f7, node3 b77dad80->5906fe4a).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d19087842d9b4204\",\"cmd-719aea89cf944cab\",\"cmd-a12721e198094745\",\"cmd-36b0866d3a7a4b05\",\"cmd-f81737b71e834014\",\"cmd-552ddfbaefa4427a\",\"cmd-c9cd17d992da4bdf\",\"cmd-1a7271b916aa4333\",\"cmd-554dcdd32baa4f56\",\"cmd-6ae904d4cc634747\",\"cmd-ab5bee1fdc7648db\",\"cmd-c6f43a5ae3624c00\",\"cmd-0712863075da4d6a\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands trace clearly to the routing configuration, connectivity verification, or the restart protocol; no failed/conflicting services, no damaged package state, and no unsafe exposure were introduced (the permissive VyOS forward filter is a necessary consequence of the stated 'reach each other on any port' requirement, applied only between the two isolated LAN interfaces, not the mgmt egress interface). Minor residue: diagnostic files /tmp/nc_recv.log and /tmp/nc_recv2.log on node3 (from cmd-6dff042382204531 and cmd-87bc6260c1bd455c) and /tmp/reboot.log on node2/node3 (from cmd-c9cd17d992da4bdf and cmd-ab5bee1fdc7648db) were left behind after testing and not cleaned up. These are small, low-risk, non-conflicting leftover files rather than broad or destructive changes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files\",\"cmd-6dff042382204531\",\"cmd-87bc6260c1bd455c\",\"cmd-c9cd17d992da4bdf\",\"cmd-ab5bee1fdc7648db\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task were satisfied with direct evidence: node1 was configured as a router between lan-a and lan-b, node2/node3 reach each other on arbitrary ports with original source addresses preserved (co